    "narrative": "For LawDog today, we are leaning heavily into the favorable matchup against Gusto, who anchors the highest-value segment of our lineup. **Geraldo Perdomo** (68.82) is our strongest play, benefiting from a massive +19% efficiency boost against a middling starter and a premium spot in the two-hole. He is followed closely by **Luis Arraez** (64.64) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.50), both of whom capitalize on the +13% skill advantage over the opposing starter and favorable platoon splits. While **Tyler Freeman** (62.19) projects lower, his +14% park factor makes him an elite start, and we anticipate **Cal Raleigh** (61.41) providing steady power production despite a tougher look against Tolle.\n\nWe are forced to navigate several marginal starts today due to the scarcity of stolen base threats, a critical component of our 5x5 strategy. **Masyn Winn** (55.15) remains a \"Strong\" start despite a lower base projection, bolstered by a +5% wind-out factor and his ability to contribute in the SB category. The most difficult decision involved **Jeremiah Jackson** (38.07), who was the first player cut from the starting rotation; he fell just shy of our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor due to a poor spot in the nine-hole and a challenging matchup against Sheehan. We are also monitoring the remaining lower-end starts like **Bryson Stott** (43.42) and **Taylor Ward** (44.15), who are active primarily for their positional utility and lineup placement rather than overwhelming individual projections.\n\nRisk remains elevated across the board today, particularly for **Gavin Sheets** (44.97) and **Taylor Ward**, who are both staring down elite arms with xERAs near or below 3.40. While we are currently carrying **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Lawrence Butler** on the IL or bench, their absence necessitates these deeper, more volatile depth plays. We will keep a close watch on **Drew Gilbert** (50.67); though he projects as a safe start against Gusto, his efficiency is tethered to the slow delivery pace of the opposing starter, and any late-breaking weather patterns in the late-afternoon window could force a re-evaluation of his status.",
